{
  "_comment": [
    "Books shown in the TOC/navigator, grouped by top-level category (matches skeletonDB.category).",
    "Codes correspond 1:1 to suttacentral.net/sc-data/structure/tree/{sutta,vinaya,abhidhamma}/{code}-tree.json.",
    "Labels are a deliberate duplication of settings/index.html's SCOPE_BOOKS/SCOPE_GROUPS (search-scope",
    "picker) — that file is client-only inline JS, not fetchable JSON, so the TOC keeps its own copy",
    "rather than refactoring a working, unrelated settings UI. Keep the two in sync by hand if a label",
    "changes. Abhidhamma sub-books are NOT listed here on purpose — their titles are read live from the",
    "corpus (see getBookTitle() in dg-light.js) instead of guessed/translated by hand.",
    "",
    "'books' is always shown. 'extraBooks' is only shown once the user has enabled the matching group",
    "in the EXISTING search-scope setting (settings/index.html, localStorage.dhammaSearchScope) — TOC",
    "reuses that setting rather than inventing a second 'show more books' toggle (owner: 'только если",
    "в настройках включена вся кн'/'абхидхамму также'). 'extraScopeCodes' names the scope tokens that",
    "unlock the group — checked client-side in public/spa/toc.js against the same localStorage key.",
    "Khuddaka is its own NIKAYA-level entry ('groups' inside 'dhamma') — a peer of DN/MN/SN/AN, not",
    "flattened into a same-level list of individual books (owner: 'кн это отдельное собрание как дн",
    "мн сн ан' — matches prod's read.php, where Khuddaka is its own collapsible heading too). A group",
    "has its OWN 'books'/'extraScopeCodes'/'extraBooks', same shape one level down."
  ],
